cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Healthcare occupancy data as an early warning indicator of infectious disease surges in the São Paulo metropolitan area, Brazil"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for the manuscript on healthcare occupancy as an early
  warning signal for infectious disease surges. Contains hourly occupancy data
  for 17 public urgent care units in the São Paulo metropolitan area
  (15 July 2023 to 12 October 2024), weekly laboratory surveillance series for
  SARS-CoV-2, dengue and respiratory viruses, and the Python pipeline that
  reproduces every figure and supplementary table: dynamic time warping,
  Granger causality testing, a z-based epidemic volatility index, early warning
  lead time analysis, and LISA spatial association analysis.
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/InstitutoTodosPelaSaude/healthcare-occupancy-warnings"
keywords:
  - healthcare occupancy
  - early warning
  - syndromic surveillance
  - infectious disease surges
  - dynamic time warping
  - Granger causality
  - epidemic volatility index
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - SARS-CoV-2
  - dengue
  - respiratory viruses
  - Brazil
